{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527080192,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NDE3MTc2MzI="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527080461,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTMzNzg1MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2541#issuecomment-391337850"},"message":"FTR: Debug level output shows, that it tries to actually add that symlink to its target instead of `top`.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527170909,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NDQzNTk2OTk="},"added":["WIP"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527171710,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTczMzExNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2541#issuecomment-391733117"},"message":"The underlying issue is that `GitRepo.is_valid_repo()` used in `_discover_subdatasets_recursively()` matches a symlink to a subdataset, when testing candidates for subdatasets. That is wrong.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527172081,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NDQ0MTEyMzc="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527172859,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTczOTgyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-391739826"},"message":"Ah, no. The input is `ssh://mars:Zoidberg` not `c:\\` in it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527173873,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTc0NTk1Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-391745952"},"message":"Sure. But I recall sth like first trying to interpret it as a path, which then would lead to assuming a relative path (since it's obviously not absolute), therefore trying to convert to sth like `C:\\somewhere\\ssh://mars:Zoidberg`. Something along these lines ... Of course my remembrance might be entirely wrong or simply outdated.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527174407,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTc0OTI0Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-391749246"},"message":"I'm afraid I'm pretty close with the guess above. `clone` does sth very similar and is NOT using `RI` capabilities first.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527175595,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTc1NjM5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-391756396"},"message":"Actually, I start wondering why the hell it raises on linux ;-)\nAnyways - I'm on it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527176504,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTc2MjAyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-391762027"},"message":"Indeed: Even on linux, `clone` concludes the target to be sth like `/tmp/datalad-test/ssh:/mars:Zoidberg`.\nWhat's causing the expected Exception is in fact the `Dataset` constructor, not some `RI` stuff. It should fail before and use `RI` to make sure, `path` is in fact a `PathRI`. I'll fix that.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527234001,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTk2OTQ5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-391969492"},"message":"Any progress? After enabling SSH tests on windows the issue reveals itself as rather wide-spread:\n\nhttps://ci.appveyor.com/project/mih/datalad-5sgef/build/1.0.91","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527240902,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTk5ODQ1Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-391998453"},"message":"Kind of.\n\n```\nIn[5]: RI(\"/home/ben/ssh://mars:zoidberg\")\nOut[5]: SSHRI(hostname='/home/ben/ssh', path='/mars:zoidberg')\n```\nvs.\n```\nIn[7]: RI(\"C:\\home\\ben\\ssh://mars:zoidberg\")\nOut[7]: PathRI(path='C:\\\\home\\x08en\\\\ssh://mars:zoidberg')\n```\n\nThe issue is twofold. For one `clone` does convert the argument to an absolute path without first checking whether it is an `PathRI`. On linux it still works, since `Dataset()` then calls `RI` which still recognizes that \"path\" as an `SSHRI` (although it's actually not a valid one anymore). On Windows the `C:\\` at the beginning is sufficient to let `RI` detect a `PathRI` instead.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527241968,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MjAwMjk3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-392002979"},"message":"Regarding other similar failures, there's even more to it.\nIn the build you linked there's `clone1.create_sibling('ssh://localhost%s/%s' % (getpwd(), clone2_), name=clone2_)`, which then fails at the end trying to interpret `\\Users\\appveyor\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\1\\datalad_temp_65tyxeij` as a port.\nSo, we build `ssh://localhostC:\\Users\\appveyor\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\1\\datalad_temp_65tyxeij` which is wrong of course. I'm just not sure how exactly the correct SSH URL needs to look like. However, that's a different issue, resulting from us using `getcwd` as something we can put into such a URL - that's not `RI`s fault.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527244604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MjAxMzQ0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-392013448"},"message":"So, my little fix solved it for the `clone` tests. Tried to solve as generally as possible by letting `dataset.py:resolve_path()` check, whether it actually got a `PathRI` to deal with instead of returning such nonsense as `C:\\something\\ssh://whatever`.\n\nLooking into valid SSH URL with paths on windows now ...","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527244636,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NDYzMjkwNjc="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1527249963,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MjAzMjc4OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2545#issuecomment-392032789"},"message":"The RI issues in your above linked build, complaining about a port `\\User\\some\\where` seems to be solved in PR #2556 as well. For comparison: https://ci.appveyor.com/project/mih/datalad/build/1.0.80\n\nThe failures are now all about a not existing `SSHManager`, which is a different issue.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527343363,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTY0Nzg4OTg0NQ=="},"status":2}]}